  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support Measure on monitoring and evaluation, audit, and communication of EU support to refugees in T&#xFC;rkiye</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to its geographic position, T&#xFC;rkiye is a prominent reception and transit country for refugees and migrants. As a result of an unprecedented number of people arriving in the country, mainly due to the conflicts in Syria, Iraq and Afghanistan, T&#xFC;rkiye has been hosting more than four million refugees. This includes more than 3.6 million registered Syrians, and 330 000 registered refugees and asylum seekers mainly from Afghanistan, Iraq, Iran and Somalia. The Facility for Refugees in Turkey (the &quot;Facility&quot;) was set up at the end of 2015 to support T&#xFC;rkiye in meeting the challenges involved in hosting and integrating this large number of refugees. The Facility had been fully mobilised, i.e. committed and contracted, by the end of 2020 and implementation of Facility-funded projects is ongoing. Following the European Council conclusions of June 2021, the EU mobilised an additional package of support for refugees in T&#xFC;rkiye in 2021-2023. This action - Support Measure - aims to cover support expenditure for the implementation of EU support to refugees in T&#xFC;rkiye and the `Facility&#xBF; and hence contribute to address the root causes of migration. It will complement and build on the results achieved within the framework of the Facility and the package of additional support, in continuation of the two Support Measures under the Facility. It mirrors the latter in terms of the components proposed, i.e.: monitoring and evaluation (M&amp;E); audit; and communication. This action contributes to the Sustainable Development Goal (17) via promoting multi-stakeholder and participatory approaches through the provision of both workshops and training courses on monitoring and evaluation, and to support&amp;nbsp;Turkish ministries and other implementing partners in the achievement of the objectives of their interventions effectively.</narrative>
  </description>
